# ==================== CREDENTIALS — NEVER COMMIT ====================
#
# This repo is PUBLIC (github.com/jeremypanaligan-cmd/GVSI-NETWORK-REPORT).
# Anything committed here is world-readable within minutes of a push (public
# repos are scanned by bots for exactly these patterns), and it stays readable
# in the git history even after the file itself is deleted. Removing a file is
# NOT how a leaked key is handled — the key is revoked in the provider's
# dashboard, and only then is the file removed.
#
# Apps Script sources are plain files that carry their configuration inline, so
# a key pasted into a .gs file is a key in the repo. Put secrets in
# PropertiesService.getScriptProperties() instead, and keep any file that holds
# one out of git by name.

# supabase-sync.gs held a hardcoded Supabase SECRET key (full server-side
# access, bypasses Row Level Security). File removed 2026-09-17; the entry stays
# so it cannot reappear by accident.
supabase-sync.gs

# Any future file whose name says it holds a credential.
*secret*.gs
*credentials*.gs
*-keys.gs
secrets.*
.env
.env.*
*.env

# ==================== LOCAL SCRATCH ====================
# Copied to .js for `node --check` (which rejects the .gs extension), plus
# local server output.
_chk.js
_inline_check.js
serve.log
*.log
# The per-thread preview log the desktop app writes. `*.log` does not cover it: the
# filename ends in `.err`, so without this line every session adds one more untracked
# entry to Source Control. It also carries absolute machine paths, so it is not worth
# tracking even once.
*.log.err

# ==================== NODE ====================
# lucide is a BUILD-TIME dependency: scripts/build-icons.mjs reads it and writes the
# committed lucide-icons.js. Nothing at runtime imports from here, so the tree stays
# out of git — 3696 icon files would otherwise be one `git add -A` away.
node_modules/

# ==================== PYTHON ====================
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ==================== OS JUNK ====================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ==================== BORROWED SCAFFOLD — KEPT LOCAL ====================
# Plannable's planning skill was copied into the root of this repo to author the plan
# artifacts. It is not this project, and none of it is needed to run the app:
#
#   plannable/  a clone of github.com/suntay44/plannable — it has its own .git and its own
#               remote. `git add plannable` writes a GITLINK, a "submodule" pointing at a
#               commit no clone of this repo has, which every fresh checkout then reports
#               as a broken empty directory. If it is ever wanted for real it has to be
#               registered with `git submodule add`, never staged.
#   templates/  the blank templates that clone ships (templates/PART_PLAN.ai.md is
#               byte-identical to plannable/templates/PART_PLAN.ai.md). The FILLED-IN
#               artifacts are what belong here, and they are already tracked at the root
#               and in plans/. Committing the blanks would vendor them, and they would
#               drift from upstream the moment it changes.
#   AGENTS.md   Plannable's own agent instructions, which open with "This repo builds
#               Plannable." At this repo's root, every future agent would read that as a
#               statement about THIS project.
#
# The rules this repo actually follows are recorded where they belong: MASTER_PLAN.md
# Notes says the artifacts are authored by hand from templates/ because the CLI is not
# runnable in this checkout.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose — the same names deeper in the tree (a templates/ inside
# some future dependency) are not this.
/AGENTS.md
/templates/
/plannable/

# NOTE: .vscode/launch.json and .freebuff/project-id are tracked on purpose.
# Do not add blanket rules for those directories — it would hide them from
# `git status` while they remain in the index.
